title:: Visual Parameters
summary:: Every key a visual pattern/event accepts, with defaults
categories:: Reference>VisualServer
related:: Classes/Vbind, Classes/VisualSynthDef, Classes/VisualServer, Guides/VisualServer

The complete set of keys forwarded from a visual pattern/event to a node. The whitelist is code::VisualServer.visualArgsFrom:: (plus code::\instrument:: and code::\view::, handled by the event types). Coordinates are normalised code::-1.0 .. 1.0:: about the view centre. Any value may be a link::Classes/Function:: (evaluated live) except envelope-timing keys, which must be numbers.

note::
strong::Naming:: the keys below are the plain names used directly in link::Classes/Vbind:: / link::Classes/Vpulse:: / link::Classes/Vline:: / link::Classes/Vlive:: (visual-only patterns). In link::Classes/AVbind:: (audio + visual in one event) strong::every visual key is code::v::-prefixed:: — code::\vx \vsize \vcolor \vstartSize \vendSize \vcurve \vwidth \vlength \vspeed \vattack \vrelease \vlegato \vsustain \vstretch \vfill \vdur \vview \vinstrument:: — so they never collide with the audio note's plain keys (incl. its own code::\legato::/code::\sustain::).
::

section:: Routing keys

table::
## strong::key:: || strong::default:: || strong::meaning::
## code::\instrument:: || code::\circle:: (Vbind) || which link::Classes/VisualSynthDef:: to use.
## code::\view:: || code::\default:: || target window symbol (auto-created).
::

section:: Geometry & appearance

table::
## strong::key:: || strong::default:: || strong::used by:: || strong::meaning::
## code::\x:: code::\y:: || 0, 0 || circle, square, pulse, spinner, live || centre position (normalised).
## code::\size:: || 50 || circle, square, live || diameter / side (px), scaled by the envelope.
## code::\color:: || code::Color.white:: || all || fill/stroke colour; alpha is multiplied by the envelope.
## code::\fill:: || code::true:: || circle, square, live || code::true:: = filled, code::false:: = stroked.
## code::\startSize:: code::\endSize:: || 10, 100 || pulse || size swept start->end over the node life.
## code::\x1 \y1 \x2 \y2:: || -0.5, 0, 0.5, 0 || line || line endpoints (normalised).
## code::\width:: || 1 (line), 2 (spinner) || line, spinner || stroke width (px), scaled by envelope (line).
## code::\length:: || 50 || spinner || bar length (px), scaled by envelope.
## code::\speed:: || 1 || spinner || rotations-per-second factor.
## code::\curve:: || code::\exp:: (pulse), else code::\sin:: || pulse + envelope (all) || easing: code::\linear \sin \cos \exp \log::. For the envelope, code::\exp::/code::\log:: are mapped to numeric curves (link::Classes/Env:: exp segments cannot touch level 0).
::

section:: Timing & envelope

code::\dur:: is the pattern delta (spawn spacing) AND the default base lifetime. The node's life and its alpha/size envelope are computed by code::VisualSynthDef.envState:::

code::
life = (sustain ? dur) * legato * stretch
envelope = Env([0,1,1,0], [attack, hold, release], curve)   // over `life`
::

table::
## strong::key:: || strong::default:: || strong::meaning::
## code::\dur:: || 1 (circle/square/line/pulse), code::inf:: (spinner/live) || event spacing; base lifetime if no code::\sustain::.
## code::\sustain:: || code::nil:: -> code::\dur:: || explicit base lifetime in seconds (before legato/stretch).
## code::\legato:: || 1 || time-scale on the total life only (NOT spacing, NOT attack/release). code::>1:: => nodes outlive the gap and overlap.
## code::\stretch:: || 1 || additional global time-scale on the total life (also scales Pbind delta).
## code::\attack:: || 0 || fade/scale-in time in strong::absolute seconds:: (NOT scaled by legato/stretch), clamped into life.
## code::\release:: || code::nil:: -> whole life || fade/scale-out tail in strong::absolute seconds:: (NOT scaled), clamped to code::life - attack::. code::nil:: => the entire life is the release ramp (original single-fade). The remainder code::life - attack - release:: is the hold.
## code::\timeDelay:: (Vbind) / code::\vtimeDelay:: (AVbind) || code::0:: (Vbind) / audio code::s.latency:: (AVbind) || seconds to defer the visual before it appears (scheduled on AppClock). Not a node param - consumed at scheduling. AVbind default makes the visual coincide with the heard audio (which is sent at code::+s.latency::); raise it to also compensate projector/display lag.
::

note::
code::life == inf:: (e.g. code::\spinner::/code::\live:: with code::dur: inf::, or code::sustain: inf::) => the node is strong::persistent::: never auto-freed, code::alpha = 1::, code::scale = 1::. Free it with code::VisualServer.default.vfree(id):: or code::freeAll::.
::

Defaults (code::legato 1, stretch 1, attack 0, release nil, sustain nil::) reproduce the original behaviour: fade code::1 -> 0:: over code::\dur:: and free at code::\dur:: — no overlap. Set code::\legato:: or code::\sustain:: to make animations overlap. See link::Guides/VisualServer:: §Envelope.
